#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:32 d9f2c7ddacb44f59937db35010b5185c
msgid ""
"**Description**: Convert protein/gene identifiers between databases using"
" the UniProt ID Mapping service. Submits a mapping job and polls for "
"results. Supports 100+ databases including UniProtKB, Gene Names, "
"Ensembl, RefSeq, PDB, ChEMBL, and more. The canonical service for cross-"
"database identifier conversion in proteomics and genomics. Example: "
"convert gene names TP53,BRCA1,EGFR to UniProtKB accessions (P04637, "
"P38398, P00533). Returns mapped IDs with from/to pairs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:34
#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:75
#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:112
#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:141 0f0a6ed6efff4caf9d752c001addcf63
#: 70412ff8ccf84e56ab8a52ed9a4f1c26 7c5fb7e7d5894fb5b56bdc836a9dbf6b
#: b4b65489fbfd4f1e991d9de95cca63e9
msgid "**Parameters:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:36 1fa7c82c97cc49dd9b8e677e5ba9e2ce
msgid ""
"``ids`` (string) (required) Comma-separated identifiers to convert. "
"Examples: 'TP53,BRCA1,EGFR' (gene names), 'P04637,P38398' (UniProt ACs), "
"'ENSG00000141510' (Ensembl)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:39 db943a39780b4918ad7fdd613c718ef7
msgid ""
"``from_db`` (string) (required) Source database. Common values: "
"'Gene\\_Name', 'UniProtKB\\_AC-ID', 'Ensembl', 'Ensembl\\_Genomes', "
"'RefSeq\\_Protein', 'PDB', 'ChEMBL', 'GeneCards', 'HGNC'. See UniProt ID "
"Mapping docs for full list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:42 46e132ef4c924594a7160135122b7526
msgid ""
"``to_db`` (string) (optional) Target database. Common values: "
"'UniProtKB', 'UniProtKB-Swiss-Prot', 'Gene\\_Name', 'Ensembl', "
"'RefSeq\\_Protein', 'PDB', 'ChEMBL', 'GeneCards'. Default: 'UniProtKB'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/uniprot_idmapping_tools.rst:45 e96cca82c5dd49caa174f1ca9c17143f
msgid ""
"``tax_id`` (integer, null) (optional) NCBI Taxonomy ID to restrict "
"results. Examples: 9606 (human), 10090 (mouse), 10116 (rat). Optional but"
" recommended for gene names."
msgstr ""

